/// Initialization must not report routine setup as a failure.
///
/// `package:timezone`'s bundled IANA database has no location keyed exactly
/// `UTC` — it ships `Etc/UTC` — while [TomTimezone.utc] is a documented
/// singleton and `fromName('UTC')` is expected to resolve. `TomTimezone`
/// therefore registers the singleton itself, which is correct and intended —
/// but announcing it with `tomLog.error` would not be. That branch is not
/// intermittent: it fires on every run, on every platform, forever, for a
/// state the code fully anticipates and repairs. An ERROR line that is always
/// there teaches a team to filter out ERROR.
///
/// These tests pin the outcome rather than the wording: no ERROR-level record
/// during a healthy initialization, the UTC registration still happening, and
/// the fact still being discoverable at debug level.
///
/// The whole file shares one initialization because `TomTimezone`'s caches are
/// static and populate exactly once per isolate — and every test file gets its
/// own isolate, so installing the recorder in `setUpAll` really does capture
/// the first access.
/// Captures log records instead of printing them.

libraries.documentation:
/// The package declares no reassignable top-level variable.
///
/// A public `var` at the top level is shared, writable state with no owner:
/// every importer sees the same slot, any one of them may replace it, and the
/// replacement is immediately visible to all the others. Nothing announces the
/// swap and nothing can prevent it, so the coupling exists whether or not
/// anybody uses it.
///
/// This has been swept by hand twice — once across the `json` module
/// (`indentEncoder`, `_namePattern`, and a merger singleton) and once for
/// `tomExecutionContext`, the ambient context in `context/`. A third sweep is
/// what a test is for. `dart analyze` does not report it: a mutable global is
/// legal Dart, and none of the lint rules this package enables covers it.
///
/// The rule is deliberately about *reassignment*, not about mutation. A `final`
/// holding a growable collection is still mutable content, and several here are
/// — `TomExecutionContext.contextMap` is filled after construction. Those are a
/// different question, decided per type by whoever owns it; what this file
/// refuses is the slot itself being swapped.

